        "original_id": "a35090fb-7213-5cb5-bbc4-e2f289027a89",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Arthur Russell, Jerry Harrison, Tony Bongiovi, Lance Quinn\n- Bands: Hecuba, Talking Heads\n- Works: Wild Combination, Psycho Killer\n- Places: Los Angeles\n\nFacts:\n- Arthur Russell was born Charles Arthur Russell, Jr. on May 21, 1951, and he was an American cellist, composer, producer, singer, and musician whose work spanned many styles.\n- Arthur Russell died on April 4, 1992.\n- In 1992 liner notes, Jerry Harrison wrote that an acoustic b-side version of \"Psycho Killer\" featured Arthur Russell on cello.\n- Jerry Harrison said he was glad Tony Bongiovi and Lance Quinn were persuaded that the version with cellos should not be the only version.\n- Hecuba performed at the Los Angeles premiere of \"Wild Combination,\" a film about Arthur Russell, and performed their versions of Russell's music there.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
